From: Grokbot <grokbot@s-w.art>
Subject: arm64: dts: qcom: vivobook-s15: AeoB CAMF rails (Phase C)

Live 7.2.2-14 still chip-id -110 on ov02c10 8-0036. Post-fail
vreg_l2m/l4m/l7m num_users=0 is power_off + probe unwind -- the
7.2 driver already bulk_get(dovdd,avdd,dvdd) and bulk_enable
before the 0x300a read. Those three LDOs are the wrong pins.

S5507QA AeoB CAMF_RES_QRD (front RGB, identical to Zenbook A14):

  PMICVREGVOTE LDO7_B  0x2AB980 = 2.801 V
  PMICVREGVOTE LDO3_M  0x1B7740 = 1.800 V
  cam_cc_mclk4_clk     19.2 MHz
  TLMMGPIO 0xED        = gpio237 reset (assert, rails, MCLK, deassert)
  SCFG_FRONT_QRD       com.qti.sensormodule.ov02c10.bin, id 0x5602300A

CAMI (IR) is the one that votes LDO4_M + LDO7_M. T14s RGB
l7m/l2m/l4m was a copy of the wrong camera.

Wire ov02c10 like Zenbook A14 (AeoB-extracted):
  avdd + dvdd -> vreg_l7b_2p8 (pm8550-b ldo7; vdd-l6-l7 already bob2)
  dovdd      -> vreg_l3m_1p8 (pm8010-m ldo3; already declared)
Keep l2m/l4m/l7m declared unused (IR leftovers). No always-on.
No driver rewrite -- supply names already match.

Signed-off-by: Grokbot <grokbot@s-w.art>
